{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"App attestation for Apple platforms: prove that requests come from your genuine app on a genuine device."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/trustpinattestkit"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"TrustPinAttestKit","modules":[{"name":"TrustPinAttestKit"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"TrustPinAttestKit","symbolKind":"module"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/cloud.trustpin.swift.attest\/documentation\/TrustPinAttestKit","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TrustPinAttestKit uses Apple’s App Attest to attest a device key with the attestation verifier you run, renews short-lived tokens, and adds them to requests for the hosts you configure as the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrustPin-Attestation"},{"type":"text","text":" header. Your backend verifies the header and decides what an unattested request may do. The framework never blocks or fails your requests: when no token is available, the request is sent without the header."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It builds on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrustPinKit"},{"type":"text","text":": set up certificate pinning first, because every call to your verifier is pinned by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrustPin"},{"type":"text","text":" instance with the same identifier, and register the verifier’s domain in your TrustPin project. Tokens can be bound to the user’s session so that a token cannot be replayed outside it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Getting-started","text":"Getting started","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AttestVerifierURL"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AttestedHosts"},{"text":" to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrustPin-Info.plist"},{"text":" that holds your pinning configuration, then:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import TrustPinKit","import TrustPinAttestKit","","try await TrustPin.setup(.fromPlist())","try await TrustPinAttest.setup(.fromPlist())","","TrustPinAttest.bindToHeader(\"Authorization\")   \/\/ bind tokens to the session","TrustPinAttest.prefetch()                       \/\/ attest early","","\/\/ Requests through TrustPinURLProtocol or the Alamofire adapter get the header","\/\/ automatically. For your own URLSession:","var request = URLRequest(url: url)","request = await TrustPinAttest.addingAttestation(to: request)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Simulators cannot run App Attest; your verifier’s operator can issue a debug token for development, set as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TRUSTPIN_DEBUG_TOKEN"},{"text":" in the scheme’s environment.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/cloud.trustpin.swift.attest\/documentation\/TrustPinAttestKit\/TrustPinAttest","doc:\/\/cloud.trustpin.swift.attest\/documentation\/TrustPinAttestKit\/TrustPinAttestConfiguration"],"anchor":"Essentials"},{"title":"State","identifiers":["doc:\/\/cloud.trustpin.swift.attest\/documentation\/TrustPinAttestKit\/TrustPinAttestState","doc:\/\/cloud.trustpin.swift.attest\/documentation\/TrustPinAttestKit\/TrustPinAttestError"],"anchor":"State"},{"title":"Logging","identifiers":["doc:\/\/cloud.trustpin.swift.attest\/documentation\/TrustPinAttestKit\/TrustPinAttestLogLevel","doc:\/\/cloud.trustpin.swift.attest\/documentation\/TrustPinAttestKit\/TrustPinAttestLogSink","doc:\/\/cloud.trustpin.swift.attest\/documentation\/TrustPinAttestKit\/TrustPinAttestClosureLogSink"],"anchor":"Logging"},{"anchor":"Classes","title":"Classes","identifiers":["doc:\/\/cloud.trus